{"term":"jog","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:9448476b89a1ca5333","definition":"An energetic trot, slower than a run, often used as a form of exercise.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jog#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:61816ac748619506e7","definition":"A sudden push or nudge.","example":"Even when I gave her a jog with my elbow, she kept staring at her French book. Even when I gave her a nudge with my knee, she kept ignoring me.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jog#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8385bb2dcef31e4360","definition":"A flat placed perpendicularly to break up a flat surface.","example":"This angle is somewhat more acute than that of the right and left walls of the Western box set; but unlike the walls of the box set, the Kabuki wall is never broken up by a jog or by a succession of jogs.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["return piece"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jog#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8f9e8fb670e6b146e5","definition":"In card tricks, one or more cards that are secretly made to protrude slightly from the deck as an aid to the performer.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jog#English","license":"CC-B